<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $80.1 mln April 16.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $80.1 mln April 16.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $80.1 million deficit on April 16 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON APRIL 16</p>
<p>Exports: $189.9 million</p>
<p>Imports: $259.9 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $310.1 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $320.2 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $80.1 million</p>
<p>APRIL DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.486 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.506 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.575 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.081 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $474 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
